Operational Learning 001 — Microwave + Refrigerator Load Conflict
Date: 2026-08-08
Summary
The Jackery was relocated to its permanent location in the dining room.
Configuration:
•	Jackery Explorer 1000 Plus 
•	25 ft contractor-grade extension cord 
•	Refrigerator connected 
•	Microwave connected 
•	10 ft extension cord installed but unused 
Observation
During normal kitchen use, Tina attempted to use the microwave.
When the microwave started, the Jackery shut off both the microwave and the refrigerator.
This behavior has now been observed on two separate occasions.
Analysis
The issue is unlikely to be caused by the new extension cords because:
•	The new cords are higher quality and appropriately sized. 
•	The same behavior occurred before the new cords were installed. 
The more likely explanation is:
•	The refrigerator compressor was already running. 
•	The microwave startup current combined with the refrigerator compressor exceeded the Jackery's available output or surge capability. 
Operational Recommendation
The refrigerator and microwave should not be powered simultaneously from the Jackery.
